= Gap80 frozen run record

Documentary publication, 31 October 2026. Source: the unchanged
`../evidence.tar.gz` package and `../historical-summary.json`. No new timing
experiment was launched while preparing this PR.

#image("historical-timings.svg", width: 100%)

== Workload, arms and accounting

The native helper computes three log-norm coefficients. Its frozen baseline
uses three trace-only polynomial products; the candidate shares a trace
functional and reversed-modulus inverse. Deterministic random-polynomial
microbenchmarks used FLINT seeds 20261031 and 80, seven alternating-order
pairs at each degree (4,096 and 16,384). Both arms include text conversion,
modulus checking and polynomial work. They measure the helper only, not
construction of an isogeny. The exact inputs are generated by archived
`bench.c`; each pair's outputs were checked identical.

The separate tile workload fixes the actual 80-bit kernel, block 4,096 and
three contexts (infinity, G and 7G). It measures one partial tile with the
Sage/Python harness and native helper. It excludes process startup and is
not a complete quotient or point-map measurement. All seven tile pairs
have equal partial-jet outputs.

== Recorded flow and exclusions

Helper: 14 paired repeats completed, seven per polynomial degree, all
retained; unpinned shared-host diagnostics. Tile: seven paired repeats
completed; pairs 1–3 unpinned, with pair 1 overlapping the fixture selftest;
pairs 4–7 pinned to CPU 0, but pair 4 overlapped the root-oracle check.
Only pairs 5–7 enter the tile summary. This rule and every receipt are
retained in the frozen package. No unsuccessful performance run is hidden.

Baseline/candidate tile medians were 3.735434/3.431381 s; the three retained
observations span 3.673185–3.751641 s and 3.384988–3.536417 s respectively.
No confidence interval, A/A spread, host-quiescence certificate, fastest-tool
comparison or independent timing replay was recorded. Pinning is not a
claim of exclusive host access. Do not promote these clocks as a current
native end-to-end or general wall-time advantage.

== Environment, checks and failures

AMD EPYC 9V74, Linux x86-64, FLINT 3.3.1; exact compiler/platform are in the
archive's `environment.json`. Native direct-root checks: 96 cases and 96
noninvertibility controls over three fields. Historical complete Sage
fixtures: degrees 19 and 10,009, six point images each, agreement with
traditional Vélu. Actual target: one 128-root tile at 32 non-kernel scalar
contexts, three backends, independently enumerated roots. These are partial
sums, not 32 full target-size map evaluations.

Historical setup failures retained in README/provenance: missing benchmark
headers (corrected), wrong initial curve twist (both tested; the +784 model
passes independent verification), read-only Sage cache (explicit scratch
cache used), and unavailable external timing wrapper (native resource
capture used). Publication-time Cargo is unavailable (exit 127); native
build, direct-root and PARI correctness checks pass. No new Rust path changes.

